How to run the command or program in the background?

  We need to use & at end of the program so it will run in the bakground.

Why we need to run the program in the backgroun?

    If you don't run the job or program in the background then user must be wait until the program completed. If you run in background you don't need to wait.

[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ vi 1.sh
                        sleep 50
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ chmod +x 1.sh
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ ./1.sh
^C[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ ./1.sh &
[1] 23649
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$

How to see the jobs which are running in the background?

Usig jobs command

^C[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ jobs
[1]+  Running                 ./1.sh &
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ jobs
[1]+  Running                 ./1.sh &
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ jobs
[1]+  Done                    ./1.sh
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ ./1.sh&
[1] 23982
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ jobs
[1]+  Running                 ./1.sh &
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ sleep 30 &
[2] 23999
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ jobs
[1]-  Running                 ./1.sh &
[2]+  Running                 sleep 30 &
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$
[1],[2] are job id's
Each job has unique job id.

How to get the jobs which are running in the background to foreground?

Using fg command we can get the jobs into foreground

[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ ./1.sh&
[1] 24116
[rakesh@ip-10-1-0-9 ~]$ fg %1
./1.sh

