How to make Partitions,format,create directory and mount


lsblk  -- list the block devices ( disks that are available for partitioning) or we can use sudo fdisk -l
once we found disk like /dev/sda1

we can use 2 commands for partitioning one 1 fdisk and another is parted(for disk sizes in TBs)

using fdisk:

sudo fdisk /dev/sda1 
it will prompt to enter a command then enter n: for creating a new partition
after that it will prompt two options one is p and e : p means primary partion this is for directly using to store the data and it is ideal for holding data of operating system and e means extended partition

after selecting the type of partition it will prompt partition number if you are doing first partition select 1(default), if you are doing nth time select n as number.
in the next prompt it will ask you to select sectors, nothing but small storage units by default it will be 2048 and we have to enter the last secotr ( select the size of the partition) then it will be created new partition

after creating partitions we have to format it with filesystems like ext4 and xfs
sudo mkfs.xfs /dev/sda
after that create a directory like /mnt/docker 
sudo mount /dev/sda1 /mnt/docker  --- (sudo mount <partion> <mount directory>
